WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.640
With rapid population growth and&nbsp;
unsustainable practices by 2030&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.480
we're projected to experience a 40% shortfall in&nbsp;
fresh water. I'm Stanford Professor Will Tarpeh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.480
and in my new course I will demystify the world&nbsp;
of water management and chemical manufacturing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.160
Together we'll explore the promise of circular&nbsp;
economies and reveal the pivotal roles that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.800
water plays from producing fuels and fertilizers&nbsp;
to making the very water that we consume every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.840
day. Unlock the future of water treatment&nbsp;
by diving into the groundbreaking realm of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.920
electrochemical wastewater refining. We'll&nbsp;
also immerse ourselves in Innovative realms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.360
of on-site treatment and autonomous&nbsp;
sensing. Join me, Professor William&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:50.440
Tarpeh and let's embark together on a path&nbsp;
of discovery innovation and sustainability.

